    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483">

                <pb facs="0935" n="811" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg811"/>

                <head>No. 479.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hunter to Mr. Morgan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-10-08"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 8,
                        1881</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 179.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Adverting to your dispatch of June 15 last,
                    No. 208, communicating the response of the Mexican Government to the complaint
                    relative to the unjust discrimination to which American trade is subjected in
                    different ports of that republic, I have now to forward herewith, for your
                    information, a copy of a dispatch of August 20 last, from the consul of the
                    United States at La Paz, respecting the case of Mr. Ramirez and those of the
                    German barks Jupiter and Carolina. Mr. Turner having been advised of the purport
                    of your dispatch, the inclosed is his response.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. HUNTER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d483-a1.xml" xpointer="d483-a1"/>
            </div>
